{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nThe force-close hint advertises a no-force path for administrative dispositions:\n> Hint: if this close is administrative (duplicate / obsolete / superseded / wontfix rather than completed work), --class <value> closes it through the attested disposition path — obsolete/wontfix with --reason=<text> ... no --force needed.\n\nBut in practice on task ticket 192c-d606-b72e-470f (brokendown-graceless-pelican, invalid premise), `rebar transition <id> open closed --class obsolete --reason=...` fails with `plan-review close gate: unsigned: no certified plan-review attestation`. A signed BLOCK plan-review still cannot satisfy the gate, so invalid-premise task tickets are structurally unclosable without operator force. Bug-type administrative closes have been observed to close gate-free through the same --class path.\n\n## Hypothesis\nThe close path recognizes only link-backed administrative dispositions (duplicate/superseded with live replacement links) as plan-review-close-gate exemptions. Reason-backed administrative dispositions (obsolete/wontfix with `--reason`) are validated later by the disposition precheck but are not exempted before the plan-review gate runs. The ordering/type predicate should treat every valid administrative disposition close as not-completed-work and bypass the completed-work close gates for all ticket types.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py -q` includes a RED regression where an open task with plan-review close gate enabled closes as `--class obsolete --reason=...` without `--force`; before the fix it raises the plan-review attestation error, after the fix it succeeds and records `close_class=obsolete` plus the reason-backed disposition attestation.\n- [ ] Completed-work closes without `--class` still require the existing certified plan-review/completion-verifier path; the regression suite proves that normal closes are not weakened.\n- [ ] Administrative disposition closes (`obsolete`, `wontfix`, `duplicate`, `superseded`) bypass the plan-review close gate for non-bug and bug tickets only after the class/reason/replacement requirements are validated.\n- [ ] `docs/plan-review-gate.md` and the CLI hint agree that administrative/attested-disposition closes do not need force and do not require a PASSING plan-review attestation.\n\n## Testing\n- RED/GREEN: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py -q`\n- Targeted docs/close-path coverage: related lifecycle tests under `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/` as needed.\n- Full verification before push: `env -u GIT_CONFIG_COUNT -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1 -u GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2 -u GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2 PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788860124465937001,"uuid":"b23f4939-c109-4f37-95e6-0be9a3f0c5fa"}